WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:11.169
Today on Hey, Flag! , we have three special guests from

2
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:16.628
Europe. Hey, Flag! Tell us about

3
00:00:16.629 --> 00:00:19.383
yourself! "I am the flag of

4
00:00:19.384 --> 00:00:24.835
Denmark. Called the Dannebrog, I am over eight-hundred years

5
00:00:24.836 --> 00:00:28.630
old. "Legend says I fell from

6
00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:36.501
heaven. In the thirteenth century, King Valdemar II was fighting a battle—and

7
00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:40.891
losing. Suddenly a red banner with a white cross fell from the

8
00:00:40.892 --> 00:00:47.777
sky. The king and the Danish army thought my sudden appearance was a sign from

9
00:00:47.778 --> 00:00:55.067
God. Everyone was filled with courage to fight even harder, and the Danes won the

10
00:00:55.068 --> 00:01:00.334
battle. "Ever since then, I have been an important symbol to the Danish

11
00:01:00.335 --> 00:01:08.257
people. People proudly fly me on June 15, Valdemar's Day, to celebrate my miraculous

12
00:01:08.258 --> 00:01:12.553
appearance. But that's not the only day Danes celebrate

13
00:01:12.554 --> 00:01:19.297
me. People often decorate birthday cakes and Christmas trees with my image

14
00:01:19.298 --> 00:01:23.774
too. "Before I go, I have something else to brag

15
00:01:23.775 --> 00:01:28.577
about. My design inspired the flags of other Nordic

16
00:01:28.578 --> 00:01:37.441
countries. Finland, Sweden, Norway, and Iceland all have cross designs

17
00:01:37.442 --> 00:01:42.252
too." Hey, Flag! Tell us about

18
00:01:42.253 --> 00:01:47.241
yourself! "I am the Union Jack, the flag of the United

19
00:01:47.242 --> 00:01:51.653
Kingdom. My design comes from the different countries that make up the

20
00:01:51.654 --> 00:01:56.760
UK. I am one of the most recognizable flags in the

21
00:01:56.761 --> 00:02:02.683
world. "A long time ago, England and Scotland were separate kingdoms with different

22
00:02:02.684 --> 00:02:06.729
flags. In England, St. George's Cross was on the

23
00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:11.379
flag. This is a red cross on a white background called a

24
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:15.001
field. In Scotland, St. Andrew's Cross was on the

25
00:02:15.002 --> 00:02:20.290
flag. This is a diagonal white cross on a blue

26
00:02:20.291 --> 00:02:26.648
field. "In 1603 King James of Scotland became the king of England, uniting the two

27
00:02:26.649 --> 00:02:30.071
kingdoms. He wanted a new flag to represent this

28
00:02:30.072 --> 00:02:34.334
union. That's when I was

29
00:02:34.335 --> 00:02:40.683
created! "Almost two centuries later, I was redesigned because Ireland became part of the United Kingdom.

30
00:02:40.684 --> 00:02:44.572
St. Patrick is an important saint to Ireland.

31
00:02:44.573 --> 00:02:48.364
So St. Patrick's Cross was added to my design.

32
00:02:48.365 --> 00:02:54.279
This is a diagonal red cross on a white field.

33
00:02:54.280 --> 00:03:00.128
Though only Northern Ireland is in the UK today, my design has stayed the same.

34
00:03:00.129 --> 00:03:04.145
"You may have seen me on the flags of Australia and New Zealand.

35
00:03:04.146 --> 00:03:10.208
In fact, I appear on the flags of several other countries and places.

36
00:03:10.209 --> 00:03:15.112
Hey, Flag! Tell us about yourself!

37
00:03:15.113 --> 00:03:19.681
"My name is the Tricolore, which means three colors.

38
00:03:19.682 --> 00:03:22.440
I am the flag of France.

39
00:03:22.441 --> 00:03:27.601
I was created around 1789 during the French Revolution.

40
00:03:27.602 --> 00:03:33.853
That's when the French people removed their monarchy and set up the First French Republic.

41
00:03:33.854 --> 00:03:41.764
My design was seen to represent the ideals of the revolution: liberty, equality, and fraternity.

42
00:03:41.765 --> 00:03:45.574
"Why do I have red, white, and blue stripes?

43
00:03:45.575 --> 00:03:47.978
No one knows for sure!

44
00:03:47.979 --> 00:03:54.125
But people who supported the revolution wore red, white, and blue ribbons.

45
00:03:54.126 --> 00:03:57.813
And the colors do have other historical meanings.

46
00:03:57.814 --> 00:04:02.752
Red and blue are the colors of Paris, the capital of France.

47
00:04:02.753 --> 00:04:07.526
Red is associated with St. Denis, the protector of Paris.

48
00:04:07.527 --> 00:04:13.679
And blue is linked to St. Martin, who was known for helping the poor.

49
00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.893
"Some people think my white stripe represents the nation.

50
00:04:17.894 --> 00:04:23.227
Others think it recognizes the old monarchy's white royal flag.

51
00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:30.872
"After I was officially adopted in 1794, France's politics remained stormy.

52
00:04:30.873 --> 00:04:34.946
Two decades later, France had a king again.

53
00:04:34.947 --> 00:04:41.550
I was replaced for a while by the white royal flag.

54
00:04:41.551 --> 00:04:44.368
I returned in 1830.

55
00:04:44.369 --> 00:04:51.455
Apart from a few days, I've proudly been the flag of France ever since."

56
00:04:51.456 --> 00:04:54.973
I hope you learned a lot from our guests.

57
00:04:54.974 --> 00:04:58.141
Your flag has a rich history.

58
00:04:58.142 --> 00:05:02.931
What does your flag mean?

